  "body": "**Found by:** the second review of PR #2659 (comment 6997335188, point F1). Related: #2597.\n\n**What happens:** on the part of #2597, material stays between the sweep of the boss ring (X 15 to 25) and the sweep of the base ring (X 30 to 40), from Top Z down to Z 10. It is a free wall 5 mm thick. No pass cuts it.\n\nThis is not a gouge, and `main` gives the same result. But a thin wall of this type can break off near the tool.\n\n**Wanted:** one of these two.\n- The contour clears the gap between the sweeps.\n- The operation says in a visible note that it does not clear the gap.\n\nA strategy choice becomes an operation parameter with a default.\n\n**Done means:** a headless test on a stepped part pins the chosen behaviour, and the shape-mask leftover check or the note is asserted.\n",
